Bag $1 \rightarrow 4 w, 5 B$
Bag $2 \rightarrow n w, 3 B (\mathrm{I}) \rightarrow$ Transferred ball is white $P(w)=\frac{n+1}{n+4} \cdot \frac{4}{9}$
(II) \rightarrow$ Transferred ball is black $P(w)=$\frac{5}{9}$ \cdot $\frac{n}{n+4}$ \begin{aligned}
& $\frac{4 n+4}{9 n+36}+\frac{5 n}{9 n+36}=\frac{29}{45}$ \\
& $\frac{9 n+4}{9 n+36}=\frac{29}{45}$ \Rightarrow n=6
\end{aligned}

